@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/g856a434cf607-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:856a434cf607ac9d8cc73d7ba9f77ca7aef27e3d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The README now leads with the seven deterministic commands rather than with extraction. }
~ The README now leads with the seven deterministic commands rather than with extraction.

It focuses on the part that needs no model and is worth someone's time today.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:856a434cf607ac9d8cc73d7ba9f77ca7aef27e3d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": It also no longer implies `stale` works on a fresh clone. }
~ It also no longer implies `stale` works on a fresh clone.

Clarifies that `stale` reads a corpus, which is written by extraction.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:856a434cf607ac9d8cc73d7ba9f77ca7aef27e3d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The model-dependent third is listed with what it was measured at, model named, in the same table." }
~ The model-dependent third is listed with what it was measured at, model named, in the same table.

Provides transparency about the performance of model-dependent commands.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": So `check` **ships advisory**: it prints findings and exits 0 unless `--strict`. }
~ `check` ships advisory: it prints findings and exits 0 unless `--strict`.

Acknowledges the limitations of the model's precision and advises caution.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The model-dependent third is honest about being weak. }
~ `extract` is honest about being weak.

Discloses the limitations of the extraction process based on measured performance.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "What did work: **two-pass agreement** (170 and 192 flags became 96, and it removed every false flag on a real commit in development), which is why `check` runs two passes by default." }
~ Two-pass agreement is used by default for `check` to remove false flags.

Improves the precision of findings by ensuring two independent runs agree.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The tool assigns labels, sources and statuses; a model proposes content only." }
~ The tool assigns labels, sources, and statuses; the model proposes wording only.

Ensures that the tool maintains control over the integrity of the corpus.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Staleness by item body hash. Reasoning is attached to code identity rather than to line ranges, so a function that moved is not stale and one that changed is." }
~ Staleness is detected by item body hash rather than line ranges.

Prevents false positives for functions that have merely moved.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Review as records. Confirming writes an attestation, rejecting writes a withdrawal whose reason unit says why, closing writes a resolution." }
~ Review is recorded as confirmations, withdrawals with reasons, or closures with notes.

Maintains a transparent and immutable record of review actions.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It ships its own instrument. `bench` measures the model *you* chose on *your* commits, and every published figure names the model it came from." }
~ `bench` measures the model you chose on your own commits.

Allows users to measure and verify the performance of their chosen models.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A cloned corpus is someone else's claim. Units carry the status the tool gave them; read `speculative` as what it says. }
~ The tool does not trust a cloned corpus as an established fact.

Encourages users to verify claims in the corpus independently.

@decision d/g856a434cf607-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/what-this-is-for.md@856a434cf607 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "If you want one sentence for why this exists: **a queryable, code-anchored record of decisions, with staleness detection, and an honest account of what the model half is worth.**" }
~ The project focuses on providing a queryable, code-anchored record of decisions with staleness detection and …

Defines the core purpose and value proposition of the tool.

